{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8rr9fqoUyMXVfbnQDR7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the analysis to `ANSWER.md`. It covers the schema after all migrations have run, checked against what the server code in `supabase/functions` actually writes.\n\n**Not in 3NF, and nothing stops the copies from disagreeing** (the ones worth fixing):\n- **`model_calls`**: `tokens_in`, `tokens_out` and `cost_usd` are all computed from the `usage` column in the same row, but each caller fills them in separately. `drafts` had the same problem and fixed it with generated columns; this table brings it back. Separately, `project_id` follows from `item_id`, but nothing checks that they match.\n- **`code_questions.cost_usd`**: this is a copy of the cost inside `usage`, and the two already disagree. When a question fails, `cost_usd` is filled from the `model_calls` total while `usage` stays empty (`_shared/server/ask_code.ts:104-106`). `project_id` vs `item_id` has the same unchecked problem as in `model_calls`.\n- **`voice_samples.quality`**: the same number is also stored in `scores.quality`.\n- **`content_sha256`** on `documents` and `document_chunks` (and `tokens` on chunks): all computed from `content`, and the hash isn't part of any key.\n- **`provider`** on `drafts` and `model_calls`: the server works it out from the model name, but nothing stops a mismatch like a Gemini provider with a Claude model.\n- **`projects.github_board_title` and `github_board_id`**: both are facts about the board, which is identified by `github_board_owner` and `github_board_number`, so they depend on those columns, not the project. Nothing refreshes them.\n- **`items.my_post`**: this is a snapshot of the founder's post, copied onto every comment under it. It's updated one item at a time, so comments on the same article can show different versions.\n- **`touches.platform`**: it should match the item's platform, but the composite foreign key covers project and person, not platform.\n\n**Not in 3NF on paper, but Postgres keeps them consistent:**\n- **Copied `project_id` columns** on child tables are checked by composite foreign keys. One of them, `idea_items.project_id`, depends on only part of its key (`idea_id`), so it breaks 2NF as well. That's the same reason `idea_items.person_id` was dropped.\n- **Generated columns**: the `triage_*` columns on `items`, `drafts.tokens_in`/`tokens_out`, `documents.is_public` and `projects.url_key` are computed by Postgres and can't drift.\n\n**Look like violations but aren't:**\n- **`voice_samples.text_sha256`** is fine for 3NF. It's part of a declared unique key `(founder_id, text_sha256)`, and 3NF allows that case; it only fails the stricter BCNF.\n- **Copies from other tables** (`people.first_touch_at`/`last_touch_at`, `ideas.asked_by`) are denormalized, but normal forms are judged one table at a time.\n- **JSON and array columns** are a 1NF question, not 3NF.\n\n`ANSWER.md` also has a suggested fix for each issue in the first group."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5540,"cache_read_input_tokens":78100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5540},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12758654-5564-441d-a699-220d2405b2b5","uuid":"3df2f754-d05d-450a-a658-02e8804b2fe8","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:47:54.135Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8rr9RTNyBkvaUDLVWdr"}
